Cause/fix: OpenRouter delta.reasoning_details text/summary fragments must be
assembled into consecutive logical blocks before persistence. The official
OpenRouter SDK implements this in src/chat/index.ts (read 2026-09-07):
https://github.com/OpenRouterTeam/ai-sdk-provider/blob/main/src/chat/index.ts
We additionally keep conflicting index/id/format boundaries and unknown
shapes intact. Encrypted blocks are never merged. Signatures are never
compared or concatenated; a late signature is retained without erasing text.
Non-stream message arrays are not merged. Replay still uses the captured
immutable envelope; no migration/rewrite of old stored reasoning.

CaptureBudget gains a bounded fragment path: validate depth and serialized
bytes before concatenation, retain the native item ceiling for distinct
blocks. JSON overhead of each incoming fragment is charged conservatively,
so a pathological fragmented stream can close early, never exceed the bound.
No repeated whole-accumulator cloning/serialization; no new unbounded map.

